<title>AUSTRIA: Austria cenbank head says EMU must not be delayed.</title>
<headline>Austria cenbank head says EMU must not be delayed.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austria's central bank chief Klaus Liebscher said on Thursday Europe's planned single currency must not be postponed beyond the planned starting date of 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;The debate about postponing monetary union is superfluous, if not damaging,&quot; Liebscher said in a text ahead of the bank's annual press conference. &quot;Austria is ready for EMU,&quot; he added.  </p>
<p>Austria considers itself one of the prime candidates for qualifying for the single currency at its inception.</p>
<p>The European Commission on Wednesday forecast Austria's public sector deficit would reach 3.0 percent of gross domestic product in 1997 -- the allowed limit under the convergence criteria -- and would fall to 2.9 percent in 1998.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom, +431 531 12256</p>
